{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["And the reason for <b>“So did Aaron do”</b> — to say that he himself was the one who lit them all his days, even though the commandment is also valid through his sons, as it is said: “Aaron and his sons shall arrange it” (Exodus 27:21). But he would zealously seize this great commandment, which alludes to a supernal matter and an exalted secret. And perhaps this was hinted to him from the verse: “Outside the veil of the testimony, Aaron shall arrange it from evening until morning” (Leviticus 24:3), for in it HaShem chose him in his lifetime. And because of this He said now as well, “Speak to Aaron, when you kindle,” and did not say, “Speak to Aaron and to his sons, when you kindle [pl.]”."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:03:36.426979276Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}